The tests look good. Coverage-wise: the `_ghPrHeadRepoFull` uncovered branches are `typeof r === 'string'` (both return variants) and `r.nameWithOwner`. The `_prListHeadRepo` in githubSource has the same uncovered branches — the githubSource tests only pass `{full_name}` or `null`.

Complexity count for `_prListHeadRepo`:
- base 1
- `p && p.head && p.head.repo` → +2 (two &&)
- `if (!r)` +1
- `typeof r === 'string'` +1
- `r.indexOf('/') !== -1 ? r : null` +1
- `if (r.full_name)` +1
- `r.owner && (r.owner.login || r.owner.name)` → +2
- `if (owner && r.name)` +1
Total comp ≈ 10? Hmm 1+2+1+1+1+1+2+1 = 10. CRAP = comp²(1-cov)³+comp. CI says 22.4: 100(1-cov)³+10=22.4 → (1-cov)³=0.124 → cov≈50%. Plausible.

For `_ghPrHeadRepoFull` (extra nameWithOwner branch, comp ≈ 11): 121(1-cov)³+11 = 13.8 → (1-cov)³=0.023 → cov≈72%.

Fix options for rework: (a) add tests covering the string and nameWithOwner branches — but CRAP with comp 10 needs cov such that 100(1-cov)³+10 < 8... impossible! comp 10 alone gives CRAP ≥ 10 > 8 even at 100% coverage?? Wait no: CRAP = comp²×(1-cov)³ + comp. At cov=100%, CRAP = comp = 10. Threshold is 8. So with complexity 10, even perfect coverage gives CRAP 10 > 8. Hmm, that can't be right — plenty of functions in the baseline have CRAP ≥ 8 but they're in the baseline already (baseline contains functions above threshold; ratchet only fails on NEW functions over threshold or regressions).

Wait, re-read: "Fails when a function's CRAP grew or a new function exceeds CRAP_THRESHOLD". So new functions must have CRAP ≤ 8 at whatever coverage. With comp 10, need 100(1-cov)³+10 ≤ 8 — impossible since comp alone is 10. So the function MUST be simplified below complexity ~7, or covered enough that comp≤8: comp 8 at cov 100% = 8, but "exceeds threshold" → CRAP > 8 fails; CRAP = 8 passes. comp 8, cov 100% → 8, not >8 → pass. But realistically: reduce complexity by extracting shared resolver and simplifying.

Actually CRAP formula: CRAP = comp²·(1−cov)³ + comp. For comp 6: need 36(1-cov)³+6 ≤ 8 → (1-cov)³ ≤ 0.0556 → cov ≥ 82%. For comp 5: 25(1-cov)³ ≤ 3 → cov ≥ 78.4%... (1-cov)³ ≤ 0.12 → cov ≥ 84.3%. Hmm comp 5: 25(1-cov)³+5 ≤ 8 → (1-cov)³ ≤ 0.12 → 1-cov ≤ 0.493 → cov ≥ 50.7%. Let me recompute: comp=5: (1-cov)³ ≤ 3/25 = 0.12 → 1-cov ≤ 0.493 → cov ≥ 50.7%. comp=6: ≤ 2/36 = 0.0556 → 1-cov ≤ 0.382 → cov ≥ 61.8%. comp=7: ≤ 1/49 = 0.0204 → 1-cov ≤ 0.273 → cov ≥ 72.7%. comp=8: ≤ 0 → cov = 100%.

So the fix for the rework agent: extract a single shared resolver with tests covering all branches heavily. A shared resolver used by both call sites gets one complexity measurement; if written simply:

```js
